+## Pure Thinglish serialization — `src/thinglish/` (Tron, 2026-10-02) — specified, not built
+
+Every component's `src/` gains a **`thinglish/`** folder beside `ts/`, `js/`, `thinglish.ts/`, `thinglish.js/`, `puml/`, `mmd/`: the model **serialized in pure Thinglish** (the grammar above), one type per file — **`src/thinglish/EAM/<layer>/<Name>.class.thing`** or **`<Name>.interface.thing`** — rendered from the **model** by the M2 target **`M2ThingClass`** (never parsed from source), generated and committed like every target.
+
+- **TH1 one file per type, derived:** every catalogued class has exactly one `.thing` file of the right kind in its component's `src/thinglish/EAM/<layer>/`; expected set derived from the catalog (CHECKED / SKIPPED / TOTAL, SKIPPED 0); seed a missing or wrong-kind file → RED.
+- **TH2 generated from the model:** `npm start` reproduces every `.thing` with zero diff; seed a hand-edit → RED.
+- **TH3 lossless except EXACTLY the held set:** every model fact appears — namespace, dependencies, kind, type params, extends/implements, attributes (type, initializer, modifiers), properties, methods (type params, params incl. `...`/`?`/defaults, return type, modifiers, TypeScript body or `;`), relationships/collections (kind, `redefines`); seed: drop any one from the renderer → RED by name.
+- **TH4 only grammar keywords:** every keyword used in any `.thing` belongs to the keyword set **derived from `ThinglishGrammar`**, each mapped per SC8 (an M3 element, an instance of `Namespace`/`Version`, or an attribute of an M3 element).
+- **TH5 no invention:** a model fact the grammar cannot express is reported (the held table), never made up and never silently dropped.
+- Parsing `.thing` back (`ThinglishParser`, F6) is out of scope — these files are its input.
+
+**Increments** (plan of record): **A** = this grammar + keyword rows + held table, `ThinglishGrammar` model, oopTester's SC8 extension — ONE atomic push. **B** = `M2ThingClass` + `src/thinglish/` for every component + TH1–TH5, with the target-listing tests' expectations as oopTester's patches.
